#
# --- the LOGIN request (was the credential-leak surface) ---
====> API Call: /api/v1/auth/delivery-man/login
Header: {Content-Type: application/json; charset=UTF-8, X-localization: en, Authorization: Bearer DYfiG2Q...}
====> API Response: [200] /api/v1/auth/delivery-man/login
#   ^ NO "====> API Body:" line — the phone+password request body is no longer logged.
#
# --- representative authenticated GETs (token query param masked) ---
====> API Call: /api/v1/delivery-man/profile?token=***
Header: {Content-Type: application/json; charset=UTF-8, X-localization: en, Authorization: Bearer DYfiG2Q...}
====> API Response: [200] /api/v1/delivery-man/profile?token=***
====> API Call: /api/v1/delivery-man/latest-orders?token=***
====> API Call: /api/v1/delivery-man/current-orders?token=***&offset=1&limit=10&order_status=all
====> API Call: /api/v1/delivery-man/notifications?token=***
====> API Response: [200] /api/v1/config
#   ^ Authorization header truncated to a 14-char non-reusable prefix; token= query value -> token=***.
#   ^ No request body, no password, no phone, no reset_token, no fcm token, no raw bearer anywhere.
